I used a (somewhat older) laptop as my primary nethack machine for a
couple of years, and was quite pleased with it.  p120, 24mb ram.

I used slackware linux on it, with X11.  The basic install, with
development, network tools, X, and some miscellaneous stuff, took up about
1gb.  (That could have been trimmed, e.g. by removing kernel source, but
it didn't matter much to me.)

Linux on an old laptop is definitely recommended.  Most older laptop
hardware is surprisingly well-supported, and there's a lot of
documentation available online.  I found it to be much faster and more
pleasant to use than win95 on that hardware.

As another poster mentioned, don't run gnome or kde.  I used twm, which
comes with the x distribution and has no eye candy.

And the vi keys only took me a couple of games to get used to.

